{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_F49IWloxUS2rG5RlRUVdcTPb","content":"1\t{\n2\t \"42\": {\"user_id\": \"42\", \"name\": \"Marta\", \"lang\": \"en\", \"sport\": \"running\", \"goal\": \"sub-1:55 half marathon in June\",\n3\t        \"zones\": {\"Z1\": \"<138\", \"Z2\": \"138-152\", \"Z3\": \"152-164\", \"Z4\": \"164-174\", \"Z5\": \">174\"},\n4\t        \"facts\": [\"Runs before work, 06:30, Mon/Wed/Fri\", \"Left achilles tendinopathy in 2024, fully recovered\", \"Owns a Garmin 255\"]},\n5\t \"77\": {\"user_id\": \"77\", \"name\": \"Jonas\", \"lang\": \"de\", \"sport\": \"cycling\", \"goal\": \"finish a 160 km gran fondo in September\",\n6\t        \"zones\": {\"Z1\": \"<130\", \"Z2\": \"130-146\", \"Z3\": \"146-158\", \"Z4\": \"158-168\", \"Z5\": \">168\"},\n7\t        \"facts\": [\"Commutes by bike 2x15 km daily\", \"Has a smart trainer at home\"]}\n8\t}"}
{"role":"assistant","content":"The bug is clear from `build_system` (bot.py:130-133): the static `INSTRUCTIONS` and the per-athlete context are concatenated into **one** cache block. `save_fact` appends to `a.facts`, which changes the athlete context, so the whole block — instructions included — misses cache on the next call. The usage log confirms it: every round right after a `save_fact` shows `cache_read_input_tokens: 0` and a full ~1000-token `cache_creation_input_tokens` again.\n\nThe fix: split the system prompt into two blocks with separate cache breakpoints — instructions in one, athlete context (which includes the facts) in another. Prompt caching is prefix-based, so a changed context block only invalidates from that breakpoint onward; the static instructions stay cached.\n\nLet me check the git state, then make the change.","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"tool_3xFAP96MoWBI2rnkz8O7WYkB","function":{"name":"Bash","arguments":"{\"command\":\"git status --short && git log --oneline -3\"}"}}]}
